load @term/seed/code/type/term
  find term

# Leibniz equality, the kernel's bottom equality, on which the observational identity type is built. Two values are
# equal when every predicate true of one is true of the other, and reflexivity witnesses that every value equals
# itself. This is the weakest equality, and the committed foundation extends it to observational equality (the identity
# type), adding function extensionality and quotients while staying decidable. The integers and the reals are
# quotients, so the math library needs that extension, but every equality reduces to this core.
#
# The rules. Reflexivity: every value equals itself. Indiscernibility: equal values satisfy the same predicates, the
# defining content of Leibniz equality. The identity type promotes this to a type of proofs that compute (see the
# identity file).
form equality
  link space, like term
  link left, like term
  link right, like term
